{"id":"NCT06798922","title":"Flap Sparing in Postoperative Radiotherapy of Oral Cavity Cancers","official":"Flap Sparing in Postoperative Radiotherapy of Oral Cavity Cancers: a De-escalation Randomized Phase III Trial","summary":"Patients with oral cavity cancer treated by reconstructive surgery with a flap.\n\nPatients will be treated in the study for :\n\n* Experimental arm: Post-operative radiotherapy with flap sparing\n* Control arm: Standard post-operative radiotherapy without flap sparing (current practice) Radiotherapy by IMRT using photons or proton therapy (IMPT)","conditions":["Oral Cavity Carcinoma","Flap","Radiotherapy, Adjuvant","Reconstruction Surgery"],"interventions":[{"type":"RADIATION","name":"Standard post-operative radiotherapy without flap sparing (current practice)"},{"type":"RADIATION","name":"Post-operative radiotherapy with flap sparing"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patient aged 18 years or older\n* Performance Status 0-2\n* Patient with oral cavity cancer (soft tissue or soft tissue-bone flap), treated by reconstructive surgery with a flap. Oropharynx cancer whose flap extends significantly into the oral cavity may be included in the study\n* Quality of resection with margins \\> 1 mm\n* Patient candidate to post-operative radiotherapy (Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy (IMRT) or proton therapy)\n* Concomitant chemotherapy is allowed (stratification parameter)\n* Perioperative immunotherapy is allowed (neoadjuvant and/or adjuvant setting)\n* Patient must have signed a written informed consent form prior to any trial specific procedures\n* Patient affiliated to the social security system\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Local flap (small size limiting IMRT modulation potential)\n* History of radiotherapy of head and neck area\n* Metastatic disease\n* History of other malignancy within the previous 3 years (except for appropriately treated in-situ cervix carcinoma and non-melanoma skin carcinoma)\n* Simultaneous participation in another clinical study may compromise the conduct of this study.\n* Pregnant or lactating women\n* Patient assessed by the investigator to be unable or unwilling to comply with the requirements of the protocol\n* Patient deprived of freedom or under guardianship","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":348,"start":"2025-03-01","pcd":"2031-03-01","upd":"2026-10-27","sponsor":"Centre Francois Baclesse","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Juliette THARIAT, Professor · 33231455050 · j.thariat@baclesse.unicancer.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"Chu Amiens","city":"Amiens","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":49.9,"lon":2.3,"c":"Alexandre COUTTE · Coutte.Alexandre@chu-amiens.fr"},{"f":"Institut de Cancérologie de l'Ouest","city":"Angers","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":47.4716,"lon":-0.552,"c":"Aurore GOINEAU · aurore.goineau@ico.unicancer.fr"},{"f":"Centre de la Baie","city":"Avranches","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":48.6844,"lon":-1.3569,"c":"DUMONT LECOMTE · d.dumont@centredelabaie.fr"},{"f":"Centre François Baclesse","city":"Caen","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":49.1859,"lon":-0.3591,"c":"Juliette THARIAT, Professor · 33231455050 · j.thariat@baclesse.unicancer.fr"},{"f":"CHU CAEN","city":"Caen","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":49.1859,"lon":-0.3591,"c":"Alexis VEYSSIERE, MD · veyssiere-a@chu-caen.fr"},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier","city":"Cherbourg","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":49.6398,"lon":-1.6164,"c":"KAO · william.kao@ch-cotentin.fr"},{"f":"Centre Jean Perrin","city":"Clermont-Ferrand","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.7797,"lon":3.0868,"c":"Michel LAPEYRE · Michel.LAPEYRE@clermont.unicancer.fr"},{"f":"CHIC","city":"Créteil","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":48.7927,"lon":2.4657,"c":"Soumya ANANE-ABROUS, MD · 0157022700 · soumya.anane@chicreteil.fr"},{"f":"Centre Georges-François Leclerc","city":"Dijon","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":47.3134,"lon":5.0139,"c":"Noémie VULQUIN, MD"},{"f":"Centre Guillau